# GPU Pool — project memory & ship habits

## Living docs (every ship)

When you change product behavior or complete a milestone, update in the **same turn**:

1. `CURRENT_PROGRESS.md` — checklist, what just happened, next picks, blockers
2. `TODO.md` — keep accurate (Done / Now / Next / Blocked); no stale “now” items
3. `CHANGELOG.md` — Keep a Changelog entry under `[Unreleased]`
4. `ROADMAP.md` — move items near-term ↔ later when priority shifts

Also touch `DESIGN.md` only if the trust model or multi-service flow changed.

## Hard constraints

- **No Docker** for this stack
- **Hermes owns agent-vms** (VirtualBox + Vagrant) — use `agent-vm-control` / `bin/agent-vm.cmd`; do not orchestrate those VMs through OpenClaw or the Discord bot
- **`host_protect` defaults ON** — leave desktop headroom; never “fix” freezes with stress tests
- **Never lag Drew’s PC** — no heavy CUDA e2e, PyInstaller stress, or continuous probe loops unless he explicitly asks
- **Never commit secrets** — `.env`, token paste files, `data/public_endpoints*`, credentials

## Scaffold & verify

- Scaffold off existing modules and docs (`TODO`, `VISION`, `CURRENT_PROGRESS`, `RELEASE.md`)
- Prefer light unit/smoke checks; invent no green checks — re-probe when updating the scorecard
- Mark agent-vms ↔ GPU Pool workspace integration as **in progress** until code clearly ships; never claim GPU passthrough into VirtualBox
